e1000: drive an external PHY through phylib on CE4100

The CE4100 GbE MAC talks RGMII to its PHY, and e1000 drives that PHY
itself: it scans the MDIO bus, resets the PHY and polls it. Features
phylib and the PHY drivers provide, such as RGMII delays from the
device tree and PHY LEDs for the netdev trigger, are out of reach.

If the device's OF node has a phy-handle, register the MDIO bus from its
"mdio" child, attach the PHY with phylib, and force the MAC to the speed
and duplex phylib reports, as for a fixed link. The MAC has no LPI
support, so EEE is disabled on the PHY. ethtool link settings,
autonegotiation restart and the MII ioctls go to phylib. Without a
phy-handle, or without OF_MDIO, the PHY scan runs as before.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
